// Real DHT1 (luma DC) plus the bit reader on grad.jpg's real entropy data
// (offset 291) -- jpg_dec.id and dec/walk.id's cases decode against this,
// and the expected symbols (7, then 0) come from hand-walking the canonical
// codes DHT1 assigns: length 1 has one code ("0" -> symbol 0), length 2 has
// one ("10" -> symbol 7) -- against grad.jpg's first byte 0x8F = 10001111.
jpg_huff_fixture() {
  jpg_dht1_fixture();
  jpg_bset(291);
} return void;
